  "question": {
    "text": "For the given close packed structure of a salt made of cation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and anion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> shown below (ions of only one face are shown for clarity), the packing fraction is approximately (packing fraction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>packing</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>efficiency</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>)\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0003_7ded6aa23bd7.png\" style=\"width: 216px; height: 220px;\" />"
  },
